WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.089 --> 00:00:04.730
We are in the middle of a global hundred year
pandemic.

00:00:04.730 --> 00:00:09.760
The highest unemployment since 1948, which
is the first year that unemployment was tracked

00:00:09.760 --> 00:00:16.049
under the modern system, the largest nationwide
protests that we've seen in a very long time,

00:00:16.049 --> 00:00:18.170
these over police brutality.

00:00:18.170 --> 00:00:23.460
And one of the highest numbers of horrifying
police brutality incidents that this country

00:00:23.460 --> 00:00:28.180
has seen in such a short period of time in
decades.

00:00:28.180 --> 00:00:36.210
And Donald Trump set a new record for himself,
sending out two hundred tweets and read tweets

00:00:36.210 --> 00:00:39.440
in a single day on Friday.

00:00:39.440 --> 00:00:47.140
The president cannot lead and instead he's
tweeting from behind his bunker fact base,

00:00:47.140 --> 00:00:54.240
which track this tweeted, we we're wrapping
the day at 200 tweets for Donald Trump, most

00:00:54.240 --> 00:00:59.260
for the account ever, period at 468 tweets.

00:00:59.260 --> 00:01:04.989
It's the most in a week for Trump during his
presidency and 74 tweets between eight and

00:01:04.989 --> 00:01:09.819
nine a.m., the most in an hour ever.

00:01:09.819 --> 00:01:14.710
As you can see there, if you're looking at
the chart along with me, June 5th, surpassing

00:01:14.710 --> 00:01:20.850
January 22nd with two hundred total tweets
and read tweets the most of any day during

00:01:20.850 --> 00:01:25.369
Donald Trump's presidency, Donald Trump is
now tweeting, by the way, from behind two

00:01:25.369 --> 00:01:28.119
miles of fencing and barricades.

00:01:28.119 --> 00:01:33.899
Much of it installed over the last week as
Bunker Boy, as many are calling him, further

00:01:33.899 --> 00:01:36.020
isolates himself from reality.

00:01:36.020 --> 00:01:41.259
So there are about five or six different relevant
layers here.

00:01:41.259 --> 00:01:44.229
First of all, I'm not president of the United
States.

00:01:44.229 --> 00:01:45.729
I just have this show.

00:01:45.729 --> 00:01:51.359
I don't have time to tweet nearly 200 times
in a day on a day where I tweet a lot, where

00:01:51.359 --> 00:01:54.670
I feel like I probably tweeted too much today.

00:01:54.670 --> 00:01:56.630
I might tweet 15 times.

00:01:56.630 --> 00:01:59.479
Maybe if I do a bunch of read tweets, maybe
20 times.

00:01:59.479 --> 00:02:02.099
And and I'm not president of the United States.

00:02:02.099 --> 00:02:03.590
That's the first story.

00:02:03.590 --> 00:02:09.929
Secondly, this day, Friday included seventy
four tweets in an hour between eight and nine

00:02:09.929 --> 00:02:10.929
a.m.

00:02:10.929 --> 00:02:11.929
Eastern Time.

00:02:11.929 --> 00:02:17.190
That is more than a tweet per hour, a tweet
