00:02:17.190 --> 00:02:21.680
That is an unhealthy level of social media
use, which raises further questions on its

00:02:21.680 --> 00:02:22.680
own.

00:02:22.680 --> 00:02:27.879
Number three, again, we're in the middle of
a global hundred year pandemic.

00:02:27.879 --> 00:02:29.569
Highest unemployment since 1948.

00:02:29.569 --> 00:02:35.180
A huge nationwide protests, huge police brutality
issues.

00:02:35.180 --> 00:02:40.939
And Donald Trump sets a record for himself,
tweeting and retweeting 200 times in a single

00:02:40.939 --> 00:02:42.079
day.

00:02:42.079 --> 00:02:43.549
That doesn't make sense.

00:02:43.549 --> 00:02:45.739
We need a leader who can lead and do things.

00:02:45.739 --> 00:02:51.319
Now, some of you will say, well, Trump can't
lead, so we're better off with him just sitting

00:02:51.319 --> 00:02:52.459
around tweeting.

00:02:52.459 --> 00:02:54.240
But the tweets are actually doing damage.

00:02:54.240 --> 00:02:55.500
It's not like the tweets are neutral.

00:02:55.500 --> 00:02:57.409
He's still doing damage by tweeting.

00:02:57.409 --> 00:03:02.599
Number four, Trump just got done attacking
